legend: {"keys": {"ar": {"field": "accessRestrictions", "into": "restrictions", "kind": "indexList"}, "as": {"field": "accessStatus", "into": "statuses", "kind": "index"}, "c": {"field": "creator", "into": "headings", "kind": "index"}, "cy0": {"field": "coverageStartYear", "kind": "year"}, "cy1": {"field": "coverageEndYear", "kind": "year"}, "fa": {"field": "findingAids", "into": "findingAidTypes", "kind": "indexList"}, "p": {"field": "predecessors", "into": "headings", "kind": "indexList"}, "ru": {"field": "referenceUnit", "into": "referenceUnits", "kind": "index"}, "ur": {"field": "useRestrictions", "into": "useRestrictions", "kind": "indexList"}, "us": {"field": "useStatus", "into": "statuses", "kind": "index"}, "x": {"field": "extent", "kind": "string"}, "y0": {"field": "inclusiveStartYear", "kind": "year"}, "y1": {"field": "inclusiveEndYear", "kind": "year"}}, "note": "Each `byNaId` row uses one-letter keys. `kind: index`/`indexList` values are offsets into the TOP-LEVEL array named by `into` — note that `as` and `us` share `statuses`, while `ar` uses `restrictions` and `ur` uses `useRestrictions`; the names do not tell you that. `y0`/`y1` are NARA's INCLUSIVE dates and `cy0`/`cy1` its COVERAGE dates, which it publishes for some series only. NEITHER PAIR CONTAINS THE OTHER: naId 604801 is inclusive 1963-1973 and coverage 1947-1964, and across 1,155 RG 59 series carrying both, coverage starts earlier in 880, the same year in 274 and LATER in 1. So a date screen must take the UNIO
  as=3 -> statuses: 'Restricted - Possibly'
  us=1 -> useRestrictions: 'Other'
  ru=0 -> referenceUnits: 'National Archives at College Park - Textual Reference'
  c=128 -> headings: 'Department of State. Bureau of Inter-American Affairs. Office of Central American and Panamanian Affairs.'
  restrictions arr sample: ['FOIA (b)(1) National Security', 'FOIA (b)(3) Statute', 'FOIA (b)(6) Personal Information', 'FOIA (b)(4) Trade Secrets and Commercial or Financial Information', 'FOIA (b)(7e) Law Enforcement']
  findingAidTypes sample: ['Folder List', 'Index', 'Container List']

